# Scripts that run on the VM must keep LF endings. Checked out with CRLF, a
# shell script fails at the shebang with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a
# systemd unit or nginx config silently carries stray carriage returns into
# values - which is how a CRLF secrets.env once produced an "Invalid
# non-printable ASCII character in URL" from a perfectly correct API key.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
secrets.env*    text eol=lf
*.env.template  text eol=lf
